# Function window design guideline

Canonical template: **Align** / **BLAST** / **Mapping** / **Flexidot** / **TE-Aid** /
**MSA plot** (`*ParamsDialog` in `tool_dialogs.py`, plus `MapReferenceDialog`,
`TreeDialog`). New tool windows must match these numbers — do not invent parallel
layouts.

Shared constants live in `repeatviewer/views/tool_dialogs.py`:

| Constant | Value | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `TOOL_PARAMS_DIALOG_WIDTH` | **608** | Outer dialog width (fixed / minimum) |
| `TOOL_PARAMS_FIELD_WIDTH` | **260** | Settings / Advanced combo & spinbox width |
| `TOOL_PARAMS_LABEL_COLUMN_REF` | `"Minimum alignment length:"` | Shared label-column width (font metrics) |

---

## 1. Outer shell

### Window size

- Width: **`TOOL_PARAMS_DIALOG_WIDTH` (608)**. Set `setMinimumWidth(608)` and keep
  resize/fit helpers at that width.
- Initial height: ~360–420 until content fit; then shrink/grow with Advanced /
  Options (see §7). Do **not** leave a tall Parameters height when switching to Options.

### Root layout (`QVBoxLayout` on the dialog)

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Contents margins | **22, 18, 22, 16** (L, T, R, B) |
| Spacing | **8** (BLAST / Mapping) or **14** (Align / Flexidot / TE-Aid / MSA) — prefer **8** when tabs + stack are tight; either is OK if consistent within one dialog |
| Alignment | `AlignTop` |

Order of children (top → bottom):

1. **Tab bar** (`QTabBar`)
2. Optional **Inputs** panel (BLAST: above the stack; Align: inside each engine page)
3. **Stack** / page content (`QStackedWidget` or tab pages)
4. **Footer** (`make_cancel_save_run_bar`)

### Tabs

- `QTabBar` (or `QTabWidget` with compact bar): `setExpanding(False)`,
  `setDocumentMode(True)`.
- Engine / program tabs first; last tab always **Options**.
- Hide the Advanced Settings button on the Options tab.

---

## 2. Parameters / engine page body

### Page root (`QVBoxLayout` on the engine page)

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Contents margins | **16, 10, 16, 10** |
| Spacing | **4** |

### Form (`QFormLayout`)

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Contents margins | **0, 0, 0, 0** |
| Label alignment | `AlignRight \| AlignVCenter` |
| Field growth | `FieldsStayAtSizeHint` (Settings option boxes stay 260) |
| Horizontal spacing | **12** (label ↔ field) |
| Vertical spacing | dialog default / modest (~6) |

Path / Reference / Define-inputs rows may use `ExpandingFieldsGrow` so the path
box stretches to the Browse button; option combos/spins stay fixed 260.

### Section structure (top → bottom)

Use bold section titles + `_form_section_separator()` between major blocks:

1. **Mode** (optional) — combine / separate / etc.
2. **Inputs** — Use selected sequences / Define inputs
3. **Outputs** (optional)
4. **Settings** — primary run settings
5. **Advanced Settings** — collapsible panel (hidden until footer toggle)

Section header: `QLabel("<b>Inputs</b>")` (or Mode / Settings / …).

Separator (`_form_section_separator()`):

- Host height **7** px
- Inner margins **0, 2, 0, 2**
- 1 px `HLine`, style `palette(mid)`

### Radio / checkbox groups under Mode / Inputs

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Layout margins | **0, 0, 0, 0** |
| Spacing between radios | **2** |

### Advanced panel form

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Contents margins | **0, 4, 0, 0** (top inset only) |

---

## 3. Label column & field column (mandatory)

Every tool must share the **same** left edge for Settings fields (and Inputs
radios). That edge is the width of `TOOL_PARAMS_LABEL_COLUMN_REF`
(`"Minimum alignment length:"`) via `fontMetrics().horizontalAdvance(...)`.

Rules:

1. Settings / Advanced row labels end with `:` (`"Map mode:"`, `"-evalue:"`, …).
2. Call **`sync_form_field_column_spacers(host, spacer_labels, forms)`** after
   build, on `showEvent`, and when Define inputs toggles.
3. Spacer `QLabel("")` on Inputs / Mode / lone-checkbox rows — **never**
   `form.addRow("", widget)` alone (radios sit too far left).
4. Colon labels are **right-aligned** inside the fixed label width so short text
   sits next to the field.
5. Do **not** pass a per-dialog `ref_label` that widens one window past others.
   Width is global only.

Also spacer-indent Advanced checkbox rows that would otherwise sit under the
section header (CIGAR/CS, HISAT2 `--dta`, FastGA soft-mask, Flexidot GFF, …).

---

## 4. Control sizes

### Settings / Advanced option boxes

- Combos and spinboxes: **`setFixedWidth(TOOL_PARAMS_FIELD_WIDTH)` → 260**.
- Same width in Advanced as in Settings (no 120-wide spins).
- Do **not** widen a combo for long item text — shorten the **display** string;
  put detail in `?` help (`field_with_help` / `label_with_help`).

### Exceptions

- **TE-Aid** full-/mid-length hit rows: ~**100** px % spin + color swatch +
  suffix text (spacing **8** in the row). Not forced to 260.
- Path / Reference / Define-inputs browse rows: stretch; Browse aligns under /
  with other Browse buttons in that form.
- Help `?`: on the **label** when the field must stay flush with Browse
  (FastGA reference); otherwise `field_with_help` after the control. For Genome /
  Database + Manage button stacks, `?` on the **combo row only**.

### Define inputs

- Use `TeMultiInputFilesWidget` (or equivalent) — path rows + Add another input.
- Placeholder style: “Click in Files/Folders or Browse…”.

---

## 5. Options tab

### Options page layout

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Contents margins | **16, 14, 16, 14** |
| Spacing between group boxes | **14** |
| Size policy (page) | `Preferred, Maximum` |
| Alignment | `AlignTop` |
| After last group | **`addStretch(1)`** |

### Group box order (when present)

1. **Right-click action** (or “Right-clicking … does:”)
2. **Executables**
3. **Process output**

Every Options `QGroupBox`: vertical size policy **`Maximum`**.

### Right-click box

- Intro line + radio list.
- Radio spacing: **6**.

### Executables box

- Spacing between rows: **8**; group margins about **10, 8, 10, 8**.
- Bundled tools: checkbox via `system_path_executable_label("Tool")` →
  `Use {Tool} from the system PATH or defined Conda environment`.
- Build rows with **`executable_checkbox_row(parent, checkbox, status_label)`**:
  - Checkbox on first line; tight tick↔label spacing (`spacing: 6px`).
  - Status on the next line, **flush with the checkbox** (no extra indent).
- Status info is always **grey** (`palette(mid)`): path, not-found, or not-configured.
- Long paths: **middle-elide**; full path in the tooltip.
- When checkbox **checked**: grey path or  
  `not found on PATH — using the built-in one`.
- When **unchecked**: **hide** the status line (no empty gap).
- External-only tools (no bundle), e.g. **FastGA**, **HISAT2**: no PATH checkbox;
  always show a named line under the last checkbox:  
  **`FastGA`: /path** or grey **`FastGA`: not configured**  
  (`set_named_executable_status`, bold name via `<b>…</b>`).
- Resolve PATH/conda with `resolve_system_executable(...)` / tool-specific helpers.
- Refresh on Options tab show, checkbox toggle, and Restore Defaults.
- Dialog height must follow the **active tab’s content** on show and tab change
  (default MAFFT open must shrink — no blank band above the footer).
- When a PATH checkbox reveals / hides a status line, **grow or shrink the window**
  to fit — never leave a pinned stack height that squeezes the groups above.

### Process output box

Always **`make_process_output_box(...)`** — never hand-roll.

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Title | `Process output` |
| Inner margins | **12, 10, 12, 10** |
| Spacing | **6** |
| Size policy | `Preferred, Maximum` |
| Alignment | `AlignTop` |

Checkboxes:

1. `Show process window while {tool} runs`
2. `Close process window when finished` (enabled only when 1 is checked)

---

## 6. Footer

Use **`make_cancel_save_run_bar(dialog, left_widgets=[...])`**.

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Row margins | **0, 0, 0, 0** |
| Button spacing | **8** |

Left (before stretch): **Restore Defaults**, then **Advanced Settings ▸**
(checkable; text **▸** collapsed / **▾** expanded; pointing-hand cursor).

Right: **Cancel** | **Save** | **Run** (Run is default when present).  
No **OK** button. `should_run()` ↔ `_close_action == "run"`.

Hide Advanced Settings on the Options tab; collapse Advanced when leaving a
Parameters tab if needed.

---

## 7. Resize behaviour

- Expanding Advanced: grow dialog height to fit; remember compact height.
- Collapsing Advanced / switching to Options: **shrink to content**
  (`_fit_to_content` / `_fit_options_content` — temporarily
  `setMaximumHeight(content)`, `resize`, then clear max height).
- Stack / pages: Prefer + **Maximum** vertical policy so tall inactive pages
  do not force blank gaps.
- Pin stack height to the **active** page when needed so sizeHint of a tall
  sibling cannot inflate the dialog.

---

## 8. Help & copy

- Prefer `field_with_help` / `label_with_help` for CLI flags and non-obvious
  settings; keep labels short.
- Tooltips on PATH checkboxes: PATH or conda env from File → Settings →
  External tools vs bundled binary.
- Restore Defaults resets PATH checkboxes to **off** (bundled) and refreshes
  executable status lines.

---

## 9. Anti-patterns

- Options `QVBoxLayout` **without** trailing stretch + group boxes Preferred →
  Process output stretches and spaces its checkboxes apart.
- Leaving Parameters dialog height when opening Options.
- Custom Process-output layouts (omit Maximum / AlignTop / spacing 6).
- One Settings combo wider than **260** “so the text fits”.
- Advanced spins at a different fixed width than Settings.
- `form.addRow("", radios)` without a fixed-width spacer label.
- Per-dialog label ref that makes Mapping/FastGA wider than BLAST/Align.
- Hand-rolled Cancel/OK instead of Cancel / Save / Run.
- PATH status without grey fallback when the binary is missing.

---

## 10. Checklist for a new function window

- [ ] Width 608; root margins 22/18/22/16
- [ ] Tabs compact (`expanding=False`, `documentMode=True`); Options last
- [ ] Sections: Mode? → Inputs → Outputs? → Settings → Advanced
- [ ] Field width 260; label column via `sync_form_field_column_spacers`
- [ ] Options: Right-click → Executables → Process output; stretch after last box
- [ ] PATH status (+ named FastGA/HISAT2-style lines if needed)
- [ ] `make_process_output_box` + `make_cancel_save_run_bar`
- [ ] Fit-to-content on Options / Advanced collapse
